<title>TURKEY: Private Turkish bank capital mkt activities halted.</title>
<headline>Private Turkish bank capital mkt activities halted.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's regulatory Capital Markets Board (SPK) said on Thursday it had suspended the capital market activities of a small private investment bank named Birlesik Yatirim Bankasi A.S, owned by Turkey's Kavala group.</p>
<p>The SPK said in a statement that investigations showed the bank had lost the general and specific conditions necessary to carry out capital market activities.</p>
<p>It also decided to cancel all trading licences of the bank.</p>
<p>--Istanbul Newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
